              "reasoning": "The value passed to `flask.redirect(bar)` is a header *name* (line 39: `param = name` where `name` comes from `request.headers.keys()`). Per RFC 7230, HTTP header field names are restricted to `token` characters (tchar set: `!#$%&'*+-.^_`|~` plus alphanumerics), which excludes `:`, `/`, and spaces. Since an open redirect requires the target to be an absolute URL (containing `://`) or protocol-relative (starting with `//`), a header name can never satisfy that condition. The list manipulation (lines 44-49) is a no-op that still yields `bar = param`. The redirect will always be to a relative path, making an open redirect impossible.",
